        "original_id": "429f2a7c-033c-5f70-8535-47bc0be8122b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benjamin Aga, Catherine the Great\n- Roles: leader of the Crimean Karaites, Empress of Russia\n- Organizations: Crimean Karaites\n- Places: Russia\n\nFacts:\n- Catherine the Great was born as Princess Sophie of Anhalt-Zerbst on 2 May 1729 (O.S. 21 April 1729).\n- Catherine the Great, also known as Catherine II, was Empress of Russia from 1762 to 1796.\n- Catherine the Great died on 17 November 1796 (O.S. 6 November 1796).\n- Catherine the Great was Russia's longest-ruling female leader and one of its most renowned rulers.\n- Benjamin Aga, also written in Karaim as Беньямин Агъа, was the leader of the Crimean Karaites.\n- Benjamin Aga died in 1824.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "72719133-051c-5112-9f8e-26f2a61647a9",
        "text": "Page: Benjamin Aga. Sentence: Benjamin Aga (Karaim: Беньямин Агъа), who died in 1824, was the leader of the Crimean Karaites.\nPage: Catherine the Great. Sentence: Catherine II (Russian: Екатерина Алексеевна \"Yekaterina Alekseyevna\"; 2 May [O.S. 21 April] 1729 – 17 November [O.S. 6 November] 1796 ), also known as Catherine the Great (Екатери́на Вели́кая , \"Yekaterina Velikaya\"), born Princess Sophie of Anhalt-Zerbst, was Empress of Russia from 1762 until 1796, the country's longest-ruling female leader and arguably its most renowned, regardless of gender (although Peter the Great was the only Tsar officially designated as \"The Great\" ).",
